      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    stock_returns = [0.05, -0.02, 0.04, 0.03, -0.01]\n    market_returns = [0.04, -0.01, 0.03, 0.02, 0.00]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    stock_mean = sum(stock_returns) / len(stock_returns)\n    market_mean = sum(market_returns) / len(market_returns)\n\n    covariance_sum = sum(\n        (stock - stock_mean) * (market - market_mean)\n        for stock, market in zip(stock_returns, market_returns)\n    )\n    market_variance_sum = sum(\n        (market - market_mean) ** 2 for market in market_returns\n    )\n    beta = covariance_sum / market_variance_sum\n\n    # Return beta rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(beta, 2)\n```",
